Devoted citizens follow Rāma chariot unturned --- Rāma asks citizens to love Bharata instead --- Rāma praises Bharata gentle fitting fear-remover --- Rāma bids citizens obey Bharata and spare Daśaratha grief --- Aged brāhmaṇas beg horses to turn back --- Rāma descends and walks on foot pitying brāhmaṇas --- Brāhmaṇas offer Vājapēya umbrellas for shade --- Brāhmaṇas plead sacrifices depend on Rāma return --- Trees and birds beg compassionate Rāma to stay --- Tamasā river appears barring Rāghava path
